{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]We were waltzing that [C]night in [C]Kentucky[C]
[C]'Neath the [C]beautiful harvest [G7]moon[G7]
[G7]And I was the [G7]boy who was [G7]lucky[G7]
[G7]But it all [G7]ended too [C]soon[C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]As I sit here [C]alone in the [C]moonlight[C]
[C]I can see your [C7]smiling [F]face[F]
[F]And I long once [F7]more for [C]your [A7]embrace
In that [D7]beautiful [G7]Kentucky [C]waltz[C]
{end_of_verse}

